  "group": "legacy",
  "title": "legacy, redis, through, strict",
  "summary": "A shared Redis with a recorded maxmemory and allkeys-lru policy (approximate LRU, and the report says so). Write-through: the new value is never published before the database commit; the writer tombstones, commits, then republishes only the committed representation. A read that begins after a write to that key was acknowledged must not return an older value; a violation fails the cell. The legacy model supplies no token, so strict freshness rests on invalidation alone or on an authoritative read.",
  "risk": "MUST record zero stale-after-ack reads and zero impossible cache values; a single wrong read invalidates the cell for performance conclusions",
